NNOOTTEESS
       These system calls are generally intended for use only by threading li‐
       braries.

       aarrcchh__pprrccttll(2)  can  interfere  with  sseett__tthhrreeaadd__aarreeaa()  on  x86.    See
       aarrcchh__pprrccttll(2)  for  more  details.   This is not normally a problem, as
       aarrcchh__pprrccttll(2) is normally used only by 64‐bit programs.

       On MIPS, the current value of the thread area pointer can  be  obtained
       using the instruction:

           rdhwr dest, $29

       This instruction traps and is handled by kernel.

